{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/812520-quotes-from-your-games-that-have-stuck","id":812520,"title":"Quotes from your games that have stuck.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-20T05:42:54-08:00","id":812520,"title":"Quotes from your games that have stuck.","content":"So, here's something that's always fun to talk about. What are the quotes from your games that have stuck with your friend/game group? And what's the story behind them? Not necessarily OP games either, any of your games from the past.<br /> <br /> For instance, in our VtM game we were a few sessions in and my fiance' was sulking a bit because his character continually was seduced by the ladies, landing him in some rough spots. As we were wrapping up the ST turns to him after asking everyone else what their character learned from that sessions events. He asked my fiance what his character had learned and in a very dejected tone he muttered 'Don't trust bitches.'<br /> <br /> Needless to say that is now a common saying among us and one of the players even had a custom shirt made that says Don't Trust Bitches across the front with the Gangrel symbol on it. It's pretty great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T07:25:03-08:00","id":812583,"title":"","content":"My girlfriend keeps a journal of out-of-context quotes from our sessions and the one that stuck the most is &quot;Goofy is actually a very complex character&quot;, which wasn't part of our game per se, but some Out-Of-Character conversation while waiting for one of the players to return. We still use that from time to time. <br /> <br /> Another one from would be &quot;I'm stuck in a mystical creature again!&quot;, this time completely In Character. Our Izanagi-Scion, who is a Biologist, got attacked by an offspring of the Yamata-No-Orochi and swallowed whole, which wasn't the first time that he got eaten. Hence the quote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T08:49:04-08:00","id":812642,"title":"","content":"Here's a few from a variety of games:<br /> <br /> &quot;Shut up and fight the dragon!&quot; -Me, shouting at my buddy who was whining about how I had 5 keys and he didn't have any while we were in the middle of a boss fight player Magic Sword.<br /> <br /> One chronicle involved needing to get past a pair of ghouls with assault rifles guarding the entrance to a building. One player says he's got a plan and everyone should follow his lead, and he sounds confident so everyone agrees. He has his character walk down the street to in front of the guys at the entrance, turns to them, and shouts &quot;Hey you jerks... punch my butt!&quot; (and when that only caused them to share a confused look with each other, he pulled a gun, fired a few shots at them, then ran down the street). For some reason, it became our groups fill-in phrase for hurling the best distracting insult your character can think of at someone.<br /> <br /> &quot;I've got a plan that would work perfectly... if you hadn't just done that thing I told you to.&quot; -The &quot;brains&quot; of the group, said to the &quot;muscle&quot; that never hesitated to do as the brains said to do.<br /> <br /> &quot;I did it!&quot; -A phrase said in celebration... of completely failing a roll as terribly as is possible in the given circumstances. A tradition formed on the first night of gaming with a particular new player, because it is what he said and how he said it when I skipped the explanation of how THAC0 works and just said &quot;You need to roll a 12 or higher on the d20 to hit the snake&quot; and he proceeded to roll a 1.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nice trick, [insert NPC's name, followed by awkward silence]&quot; -Me, in character, playing a character that liked to banter during combat, and realizing mid-sentence I had completely nothing in the tank at that particular moment. My group continues to quote it (as &quot;Nice trick, The Arbiter,&quot; because it happened to be during a game of Exalted and the NPC had some word-salad name that began that way), mostly because they are used to me being the guy in the group that is lightning fast with witty comebacks and so ready to improvise that I've not been caught with nothing to say any other times in the decade they've all known me.<br /> <br /> Player 1: &quot;We came on a message of peace.&quot; Player 2: &quot;Eugh.&quot; And because we are full grown children, a simple misspoken &quot;on&quot; where &quot;with&quot; was intended in this situation gives us near-endless laughs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T08:51:56-08:00","id":812644,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of happily yelling 'I did it!' when you botch something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:24:34-08:00","id":812671,"title":"","content":"&quot;Don't worry it will grow back.&quot; When discussing the addition of a new Pack Mate while our Totem Crow was thinking his eyes looked tasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:20:29-08:00","id":812745,"title":"","content":"D&amp;D game, my character was starting to become crazy and he blamed everything on his friends.<br /> <br /> &quot;Let me get this straight. You were tortured by strange black, hooded figures, left to rot in a dungeon for days and were saved by the god of <i>Lies and Treacheries</i>, who told you <b>we</b> were to blame for it... AND YOU BELIEVED HIM!?&quot;<br /> <br /> From that point on &quot;And you believed him?&quot; became a catchphrase in almost all of our games in which some pretty obvious lie somehow succeeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:34:15-08:00","id":812757,"title":"","content":"&quot;Don't worry. I'll be right behind you!&quot; Our Night Caste, when our circle is about to do something dangerous and stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:33:17-08:00","id":812788,"title":"","content":"There was another that stuck with my group while we were playing Dark Heresy at some point someone asked it what time it was in-game and the GM asked if anyone was wearing a watch. Again, my fiance popped up saying 'I assume we all have watches, it's the future.' <br /> And now we always like to say 'it's the future' when someone wants to know what time it is or doesn't have some basic thing that we didn't physically write down before the session.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10575-lilappleblossom","name":"lilappleblossom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:43:32-08:00","id":812799,"title":"","content":"&quot;You'll see Hell soon, boy!&quot; - friend playing a Tzimisce Voivode<br /> &quot;How far is this guy on the horse?&quot; - same friend, out of character<br /> &quot;About twenty feet&quot; - me<br /> &quot;Can this axe be thrown?&quot; -same friend, out of character<br /> &quot;Yeah. Want me to roll that?&quot; - me. The friend nods, I roll all 8s, 9s and 10s.<br /> &quot;YOU DON'T LOOK LONG FOR THIS WORLD WITHOUT YOUR STEED, MY IDIOT FRIEND.&quot; - Friend, In Character. Me, realizing I helped him kill a horse with a throwing axe.<br /> <br /> &quot;THAT is the Great Serpent of Pangaea?? I bet it's bones could make badass fetishes.&quot; - Finn aka Bada the Savior<br /> <br /> &quot;Why the fuck would a vampire need TWO manatees??&quot; - Matthias, Ventrue Pimpenstein<br /> <br /> &quot;Fuck it. I'm gonna just become a replacement barmaid and get paid. We don't need to bring back a good looking woman. I just need to serve drinks. I can spy on folks, too&quot; - my current DAV 20 character, just before making a terrible roll on Obfuscate 3 and becoming his own ugly sibling instead.<br /> I gave up trying to wench after that.<br /> <br /> I have probably so many more. These I can drop into conversation with the group like chuckle grenades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":380,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","user":"AzraelFirestorm","date":". 01-20-2016, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:26:32-08:00","id":812855,"title":"","content":"I'm playing a fifth edition D&amp;D game. I'm a bard. One of my cantrips is <i>vicious mockery</i>, which lets you insult someone so hard they take psychic damage and suffer dice penalties to doing shit.<br /> <br /> We were fighting the bald-headed leader of a demon-worshipping cult and I had no ranged weapons, so I cast <i>vicious mockery</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you say to him?&quot; my DM asked.<br /> <br /> &quot;I yell at him, 'Your head looks like the cum-bubble your mom farted last night after I came in her butthole,'&quot; I said.<br /> <br /> The game stopped for ten minutes, and I kept getting texts about it. Now every time we have a new session, people ask me what anal-related insult I have prepared for my spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:42:30-08:00","id":813047,"title":"","content":"Referring, in character, to one of the other PC's in my old Forsaken game. &quot;He's actually a were-cat, he turns into a giant pussy at the first sign of danger.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:13:06-08:00","id":813124,"title":"","content":"A DnD classic from back in the day about 25 years ago -- the only game where the following can be said with a straight face:<br /> &quot;I climb into the dragon's sinus cavity...&quot; We all looked at our game-mate and it took us several seconds to realize just how *utterly absurd* the imagery invoked -- let alone the action the described -- actually was... (Note: he crit'd, doing the damage necessary to finish the beast... leaving us all to carry on the wisdom of the bard who noted &quot;When it doubt -- climb up the snout!&quot; ) Again, only in DnD... (To clarify: the dragon was grounded and cornered in a crevasse at the side of a caldera, and circumstances made the action plausible contextual to everyone's positioning at the time... but still... only in DnD...) <br /> <br /> A DA/Ravenloft hybrid (which I've been running on-an-off since the 90s) -- a couple of the PCs had (for real-life years and decades-long game time) essentially been courtesans for a number of powerful/influential people (one of the PCs had started out as a &quot;common&quot;, gutter-side whore). One of the public houses they occasionally frequented was &quot;The Brazen Hussy&quot;; this led to the occasional re-cap of past sessions starting as (in the voice of a narrator at the beginning of a TV show): &quot;Previously, on Brazen Hussies...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You have <i>no idea</i> how many dots in Faggotry I have...&quot; Meta-in-character-but-as-the-player comment in response to what made *his* character (the character, himself) the more viable candidate for dealing with the pomp and circumstance surrounding a layered-class gathering of &quot;higher&quot; and &quot;lower&quot; born persons (mostly contextual to Vampire, but with some other splats involved), and whether or not he (the character as well as the player) would have the multi-faceted style, panache, wit and humor to handle such a gathering. (The debate ended then-and-there -- everyone was convinced that he, both the player and the character, had what it took to &quot;make that shit *wyrq*, bytch...&quot;. A fun time was had by all...)<br /> <br /> &quot;Can't we just *ask* the Lich to let us borrow his phylactery so we can research the link it has to the Etruscan necromantic ritual we've been trying to formulate...?&quot; (The question was asked by the player -- who should have known better, being a gamer for many years at that point -- with completely flat intention and sense of legitimate inquiry. The players and the GM just stared at him for literally several seconds -- nobody knew how to &quot;take&quot; the obvious-to-us/anybody-with-any-sense facet of the situation that (apparently) &quot;totes legit&quot; was oblivious in the mind of the player. Needlessly to say, the answer was *no*. It did, though, become the running-joke to go &quot;Can't we just [x] the [y] for [z] reasons?&quot; when said statement was of equal relative absurdity to the first one that started the ball rolling...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T00:54:03-08:00","id":813968,"title":"","content":"JJF, if my humerus weren't genuinely injured right now, I'd say you tickled my funny bone. That post had me rolling. I might have to steal &quot;Faggotry&quot; as an actual Ability stat for my socially abhorrent Hunter game. Jim...good god, man. You didn't half ass that. You used the whole of the ass. This is my new favorite thread and may it never die.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to play my next session now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T08:29:43-08:00","id":814144,"title":"","content":"My wife and I have one that has stayed with us for so many years that I can't even remember the first time it was used. It crops up at least once per chronicle. Generally, the setup comes when one character is worried or complaining about a task being too hard. The response by player or NPC is inevitably &quot;Nothing worth doing is easy... Except Veronica.&quot; This is the response even in games that lack a character called Veronica.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T15:35:41-08:00","id":814496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AzraelFirestorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/812520-quotes-from-your-games-that-have-stuck?p=813968#post813968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jim...good god, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my few talents in life is that if I ever have to open my mouth, I can be pretty sure something will fall out of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T17:55:01-08:00","id":814562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/812520-quotes-from-your-games-that-have-stuck?p=814496#post814496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my few talents in life is that if I ever have to open my mouth, I can be pretty sure something will fall out of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You really have to stop giving me straight lines to work with, if I wasn't a moderator....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T03:21:22-08:00","id":814750,"title":"","content":"&lt;Dusk_Rose&gt; I exploded this one time, that kinda sucked but ah got over it. - From a friend's PC in an old game of Exalted of mine... she was basically a Texan Gunslinger Infernal.<br /> <br /> `HG`: It's the PRETTIEST skeleton. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> - OOC comment after I asked how pretty the skeleton was after the wizard set it on fire in a 13th Age game. Since we all know, firelight makes everything prettier.<br /> <br /> [Benton_Hall] &quot;Love at first blood, hmm?&quot; - Benton discussing my PC, Henry Irons, and his younger sister Emma having a sword duel in an alley in Victorian London at night... which resulted in a huge crush between the two teens after they mutually struck each other for first blood in the same second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T19:20:39-08:00","id":815822,"title":"","content":"There's a rule in Monsterhearts that you can't just say that you do a move, you have to say what you actually do in character that triggers the move. So, for the basic move <b>turn someone on</b> which every character can trigger, you have to describe the sexy thing you're doing which leads to the <b>turn someone on</b> roll. Pretty straightforward, right?<br /> <br /> The first time I ran M&lt;3 at grad school, the Vampire's player had some trouble with this one. His character had a really mercenary attitude towards sex and relationships. So we had a couple of variations of this conversation.<br /> <br /> Vampire: \u2026 so after I walk out of the burning dormitory, I go to Emma's room and turn her on.<br /> Me &amp; Other Players: You can't just say &quot;I turn her on.&quot;<br /> Vampire: Why not?<br /> Me &amp; Other Players: [five minutes of half-competent explanation which amounted to &quot;Say a sexy thing that you do that would turn someone on if you did it&quot;]<br /> Vampire (rolling eyes): Fine. I, uh \u2026 lean sexily against the wall.<br /> Me: \u2026 close enough, roll with hot.<br /> <br /> After the second time the Vampire exasperatedly and impatiently leant against a wall, any time in any game that any character said or did something sexy, they incorporated &quot;leaning sexily against the wall.&quot; Whatever the hell that means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T23:38:25-08:00","id":815929,"title":"","content":"A new one, but when you break two of the Traditions, piss off half of Constantinople and start fights with two elders and straight up fuck with the only Giovani in town in a single in-game night of DAV, making your entire group laugh at you and themselves for associating with you, it will probably have staying power:<br /> <br /> &quot;JOEY DUN GOOFED!&quot;<br /> - the ST/buddyroo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T09:16:51-08:00","id":819313,"title":"","content":"One more from one of my games, presented without context: <br /> <br /> &quot;Whats 'Blackjack and Hookers' in Ancient Greek?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T16:55:46-08:00","id":820037,"title":"","content":"I was playing a giant wendigo in a WtA game and my first session we were dealing with this riot that had errupted so violently (our theuruge decided to bottle a spirit of aggression and let it loose so we could have a distraction.) These fomori came out of the building we were about to attack and I went into chrinos, succeeded in ripping the entire turret off the top of an APC and beat about 10 Black Spiral Dancers to death with it and a large group of horribly deformed explosive fomori. When we got back to the caern, the old gurahl who hung out there asked what happened and we told him. And the quote that was used was &quot;So let me get this straight, you ripped a turret off of a tank and played baseball with explosive fomori? Is that how subtelty works in the swamp you're from?&quot;<br /> <br /> Chief, my first ever WoD character, went on a crazy crime spree 15minutes into the game, mostly because of how the ST handled the situation. (I was panhandling in front of a hospital wearing just a pair of hospital pants and a t short and a cop stole my money out of the can because I wouldn't speak. I threw tin can at him, connected and rolled so many successes I did 6 bashing) I went and hid in the museum after beating the cop into unconsciousness with his own gun and tried to hide in an exhibit about cavemen. When the other players got more involved with me the lawyer character asked what I did to get aggravated assault on a law enforcement officer and showed him the crumpled can. It's not a quote but after that, people went far out of their way to kill or maim people with bizarre objects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}